Description: build projects with the V\OS layout and flag set
 Project loading, platform detection and the command builders still
 assumed the legacy tree. This maps the project-file tokens onto the V\OS
 header and library locations, reports the modern-gcc platform flavour for
 this system, passes the system compiler flag set (/etc/vos.specs - the
 same file the makefile-engine puts on CFLAGS) to every compile and
 dependency scan so angle-included headers resolve, lists libroot when
 linking (the dynamic linker here does not resolve it through the
 interface kit library), and keeps /system header paths out of the
 per-file dependency list. Two debug prints without format strings are
 also made explicit so they survive the distribution's
 format-security-as-error flag.
Author: VitruvianOS Ports <ports@vitruvian.invalid>
Forwarded: no
Origin: upstream https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Paladin @ 5b7c442bd68eb3e04ce2b5b780eb2314db3b977a

